==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|p|e}}

===Etymology===
Of [[Baltic-Finnic]] root {{term/t|fiu-fin-pro|*pereh}}, from {{term/t|fiu-fin-pro|*pereš}} <ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2005}}</ref>, cognate with Karelian {{term|lang=krl|pereh}}, Estonian and Votic {{term|lang=et|pere}}, [[Võro]] {{term|lang=vro|pereq}}, Veps {{term|lang=vep|peŕeh}}, Livonian {{term|lang=liv|perē}}. Believed to come from the same [[Proto-Uralic]] root as {{term|lang=fi|perä||rear}}, referring to the background of a person, compare {{term|lang=fi|alkuperä||origin}}, {{term|lang=fi|peräisin||originating from}}. First written appearance is from 1548 in the Finnish version of Sweden's {{term|lang=fi|maanlaki||law of the country}} translated by a cleric known as {{w|lang=fi|Herra Martti}}.

